title: A file deleted on disk is listed in Source Control as a deletion with the files that changed, can be staged and unstaged, and comes back when the deletion is discarded
folders: git-rename-staged
limit: 60
forbid-log: WARN.*script
forbid-log: script: ignoring
expect-file: git-rename-staged/src/removed.rs :: ^pub fn removed\(\) \{\}\n$

wait 3500
left changes
wait 1200
mark a-deletion-listed
wait 450
git stage src/removed.rs
wait 1200
mark b-deletion-staged
wait 450
git unstage src/removed.rs
wait 1200
git discard src/removed.rs
wait 600
answer Discard
wait 1500
mark c-file-is-back
wait 450
quit
